# noramedi-opscheck.env.example — F3-OBS-002
#
# This is a NAME-ONLY documentation template. It is safe to commit because
# every value below is either blank or a placeholder — NEVER fill in real
# values here or in any file that gets committed to this repository.
#
# On the production host, copy the variable names below into a real,
# NOT-git-tracked file at /etc/noramedi/opscheck.env, owned root:root, mode
# 0600, and fill in the real ping URLs there only. That file is what
# ops/systemd/noramedi-opscheck.service's `EnvironmentFile=` directive
# loads. Proposed host commands:
#
#   install -o root -g root -m 0600 /dev/null /etc/noramedi/opscheck.env
#   $EDITOR /etc/noramedi/opscheck.env   # paste real values, save
#   systemctl restart noramedi-opscheck.timer   # picks up the new env file
#
# Each of the three *_PING_URL variables is a secret operational credential
# (a dead-man's-switch ping URL from the external monitoring provider, e.g.
# Healthchecks.io-style). Anyone holding one can spoof a "healthy" signal
# and suppress a real alert for that check. Treat exactly like a database
# password or API token:
#   - never commit a real value to git
#   - never paste a real value into a docs/program evidence file, a PR
#     body, a screenshot, a ClickUp comment, or a Slack/Teams message
#   - evidence for F3-OBS-002 may record variable NAMES, check NAMES,
#     timestamps, and HTTP result codes — never the URL/UUID/key itself

# Ping URL for the pm2 check (noramedi-api + noramedi-worker PM2 status).
NORAMEDI_OPSCHECK_PM2_PING_URL=

# Ping URL for the disk-usage check.
NORAMEDI_OPSCHECK_DISK_PING_URL=

# Ping URL for the backup-freshness check.
NORAMEDI_OPSCHECK_BACKUP_PING_URL=

# Optional tuning — safe to set here, not secret. Defaults shown (scripts/noramedi-opscheck.sh).
# NORAMEDI_OPSCHECK_DISK_THRESHOLD_PERCENT=90
# NORAMEDI_OPSCHECK_BACKUP_MAX_AGE_HOURS=30

# Only ever set on the host temporarily, for the DRILL B controlled test
# (see the F3-OBS-002 evidence doc) — comma-separated check names
# (pm2,disk,backup) whose PING is skipped while the local check still runs
# and is still reported. Leave unset in normal operation.
# NORAMEDI_OPSCHECK_SUPPRESS_PING=
